      {
        "source": "PMID8282725",
        "judgment": "Full-length pSU11S/pSU11R expressed in DZ225; BaeS in4Murea-washed membrane fraction and BaeR in45percent-saturation ammonium-sulfate cytosol. Fig8A/C supports ATP-dependent labeling and authors presumed cognate transfer, with vector control; not a purified pair, exact donor-loss assay, site-specific proof or physiological ligand experiment. H250/D61 conserved candidate sites inFig6. pSN25 truncated BasS is separate; OmpR cross-phosphorylation is separate."
      },
      {
        "source": "PMID12107134",
        "judgment": "Constructs distinct: altered pTrcBaeR last8residues replaced by17vectorresidues; intact pBADBaeR; separate CterminalValAspHis6 protein. Wholecell resistance/accumulation is contextual (notably deltaacrAB), promoter reporter and purified-tagged-protein EMSA support mdtA regulation. BaeS deletion does not abolish overexpression phenotype and binding preparation probably unphosphorylated. No obligatoryphosphorylation claim; no MdtD requirement or measured native oligomer stoichiometry."
      },
      {
        "source": "PMID21515766",
        "judgment": "Read all79articleblocks, all44bibliography entries, four figures and imageTable2. WT/mutant reporters support condition-specific flavonoid,tungstate,zinc/highindole induction; not direct BaeS ligand binding. MdtA complementation supports efflux-related interpretation, not purified substrate transport. Biofilm tests use2K1056/500uMindole and do not justify universal lack of BaeSR effect. Introductory dimer/activation assertions are not directly measured here."
      }
